                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            was introduced in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger93"} Axelrod-Singer 93, p. 5-6
            %a{:href => "#FultonMacPherson94"} Fulton-MacPherson 94
            and an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            defined on it by
            %a{:href => "#GetzlerJones94"} Getzler-Jones 94
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich97"} Kontsevich 97
            = succeed "," do
              %em Fulton-MacPherson operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weakly equivalent
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+n-disk+operad"} little n-disk operad
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salvatore01"}> Salvatore 01, Prop. 4.9
            ), hence a model for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/En-operad"} En-operad
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            as well as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            itself of the Fulton-MacPherson operad it
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complexes"} graph complexes
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToGraphComplexes"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
            computation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            that motivated the compactified configuration space, this way, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger91"} Axelrod-Singer 91
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger93"} Axelrod-Singer 93
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            serve to exhibit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dg-algebra"} formality
            of the Fulton-MacPherson operad, and hence also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formality+of+the+little+n-disk+operad"} formality of the little n-disk operad
          %p
            To see the nature of the Axelrod-Singer-Fulton-MacPherson compactification of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space
            of exactly 2 points in a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+two"} Z/2
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} (d-1)-sphere
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Conf_2( \mathbb{R}^d )
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  S^{d-1}/(\mathbb{Z}/2)
          %p
            this being the sphere of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction+of+a+vector"} directions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
            pointing from one of the two points to the other. This means that the configuration space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf_n( \mathbb{R} )
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            points is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalent"} homotopy equivalent
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of one such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} (d-1)-sphere
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction+of+a+vector"} directions
            for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of points and various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+intervals"} open intervals
            encoding the relative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            between the points.
          %p
            The
            %em Fulton-MacPherson compactification
            is the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} (d-1)-spheres
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+intervals"} open intervals
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+intervals"} closed intervals
          %p
            This means that a point on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            of the Fulton-MacPherson compactification corresponds to a would-be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration
            of points where some of the points have formally vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            to each other, while still remembering a relative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction+of+a+vector"} direction
            to each other.
          %p
            More abstractly one may sum this up succinctly by saying that the ASFM-compactification is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/blowup"} blowup
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"} fat diagonal
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            of the base space with itself.
          %p
            In the literature these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            configurations are often referred to in terms of “infinitesimally close points”. While there may be some formal relation to actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhoods"} infinitesimal neighbourhoods
            in (for example)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or manifolds with corners (in some suitable sense), not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            in any of the usual senses.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n, d \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of configurations of
            %em ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuples"} n-tuples
            of points in the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embeddings+of+topological+spaces"} embeddings of topological spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Emb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo )
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Emb( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d )
                  \\;\subset\;
                  \\left(
                  \\mathbb{R}^d
                  \\right)^n
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translations
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale+transformations"} scale transformations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            canonically on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            and hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+action"} diagonally
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Emb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Emb( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+space"} quotient topological space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Emb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Emb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ⋊
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Emb( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d )
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Emb( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d )/ \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}
          %p
            is clearly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
            to the original space.
          %p
            But now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            this quotient space canonically carries the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            (in fact of a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi Emb
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo ⋊
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi n
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  dim
                  \\left(
                  Emb\left( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d \right)/\left( \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}\right)
                  \\right)
                  \\;=\;
                  n \cdot d - d - 1
          %p
            while for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \leq 1
            the quotient is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
            0).
          %p
            Now for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \neq j \in \{1, \cdots, n\}
            of distinct indices, consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
          #eq:ProjectionsToBoundarySpheres.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Emb
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo ⋊
                            %msub
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mo &gt;
                                %mn 0
                            %mi right
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi θ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi j
                              %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi j
                              %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Emb\left( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d \right)/\left( \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}right)
                  \\right)
                  \&amp;\overset{\theta_{i j}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  S^{d-1} \subset \mathbb{R}^d
                  \\\
                  (x_1, \cdots, x_n)
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\frac{
                  x_j - x_i
                  }{
                  {\vert x_j - x_i\vert}
                  }
                  }
          %p
            which takes each configuration to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction"} direction
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
            between the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %p
            Moreover, for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple"} triple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j,k
            of mutually distinct indices, consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Emb
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo ⋊
                            %msub
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mo &gt;
                                %mn 0
                            %mo )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi δ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi j
                              %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Emb\left( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d \right)/\left( \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}\right)
                  \&amp;\overset{\delta_{i j k}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  (0,\infty) \subset [0,\infty]
                  \\\
                  (x_1, \cdots, x_n)
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\frac{ {\vert x_i - x_j\vert} }{ {\vert  x_j - x_k \vert} }
                  }
          %p
            which takes each configuration to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ratio"} ratio
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            between the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Together these functions induce one total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
          #eq:EmbeddingOfTheOrderedConfigurationSpace.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Emb
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⋊
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                    %mo )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Emb\left( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d \right)/\left( \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}\right)
                  \\overset{ (\theta_{i j}, \delta_{i j k}) }{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\left( S^{d-1} \right)^{ n(n-1) }
                  \\times [0,\infty]^{ \left(  n(n-1)(n-2) \right) }
          %p
            from the ordered configuration space into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of all these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} (d-1)-spheres
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intervals"} intervals
          %p
            A moment of reflection shows that every ordered configuration modulo translation and rescaling, hence every point on the left, may be uniquely reconstructed from its direction vectors and distance ratios, hence from a point on the right, hence that this function is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            onto its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sinha03"}> Sinha 03, lemma 3.18
            ).
          #FultonMacPhersonCompactification.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Fulton-MacPherson compactification)
            %p
              The
              %em Fultan-MacPherson compactification
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space
              of ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuples"} n-tuples
              of points in the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EmbeddingOfTheOrderedConfigurationSpace"} (2)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi Emb
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi d
                            %mo ⋊
                            %msub
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mo &gt;
                                %mn 0
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\overline{ \iota\left(
                    Emb\left( \{1, \cdots, n\}, \mathbb{R}^d \right)/\left( \mathbb{R}^d \rtimes \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}\right)
                    \\right) }
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14, Def. 5.1
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
            still canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FM
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d)
            and hence the FM-compactification of the actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf_n(\mathbb{R}^d)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Conf
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ¯
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi FM
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{Conf_n(\mathbb{R}^d)}
                  \\;=\;
                  FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d)/\Sigma(n)
                  \\,.
          %h2#Pictorial Pictorial notation
          %p
            By the above, the points on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            of a Fulton-MacPherson compactification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FultonMacPhersonCompactification"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triples"} triples
            of points in space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            between two of them is “vanishing in ratio to the distance of both to the third”.
          %p Hence where a configuration of two points in space looks like
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FultonMacPherson1.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %p a configuration of such a boundary case of three points may be visualized as
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FultonMacPherson2.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %p where the “funnel” might be thought of as an infinite magnifying glass held to the location of the second point and revealing that it really consists of two points of vanishing distance to each other, relative to their joint distance to the remaining point.
          %p In this fashion, for instance a boundary point in the Fulton-MacPherson compactification depicted as follows
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FultonMacPherson3.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %p would consist of
          %ul
            %li
              %p points 3, 4 and 5 being arbitrarily close to each other with respect to their distance to points 1, 2 and 6
            %li
              %p points 3 and 5 also being arbitrarily close to each other with respect to their joint distance to 4
            %li
              %p points 1, 2 and 6 being arbitrarily close to each other in comparison to their joint distances to 3, 4 and 5
            %li
              %p points 1 and 2 also being arbitrarily close to each other with respect to their joint distance to 6.
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14, Figures 3 and 4
          %p
            This pictorial notation was introduced in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sinha03"} Sinha 03
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on the Fulton-MacPherson compactifications.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_the_little_disk_operad
            Relation to the little
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #WeakEquivalenceToLittleNDiskOperad.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The Fulton-MacPherson operad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FM_\bullet\left( \mathbb{R}^d\right)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weakly equivalent
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
              with respect to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+n-disk+operad"} little d-disk operad
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salvatore01"}> Salvatore 01, Prop. 4.9
            , summarized as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14, Prop. 5.6
          %h3#deRhamCohomology de Rham cohomology
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi FM
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d))
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi FM
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet_{dR}( FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d) )
            of Fulton-MacPherson compactifications.
          #SphereClassGeneratorsOfDeRhamCohomology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{N}
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
              of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              (number of points) and consider the Fulton-MacPherson compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d)
              from Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FultonMacPhersonCompactification"}
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dvol
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dvol_{\left(S^{d-1}\right)}
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\Omega^\bullet\left( S^{d-1} \right)
            %p
              be the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
              on the standard
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} d-sphere
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \neq j \in \{1, \cdots, n\}
              two distinct point labels, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo )
                      %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi FM
                        %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi d
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_{i j}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left(\theta_{i j}\right)^\ast\left( dvol_{\left( S^{d-1}\right)}\right)
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\Omega^\bullet\left( FM_n\left(\mathbb{R}^d\right) \right)
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
              of this standard volume form along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{i j} \;\colon\; FM_n\left( \mathbb{R}^{d}\right) \longrightarrow S^{d-1}
              from
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProjectionsToBoundarySpheres"} (1)
          #DeRhamCohomologyOfFMCompactification.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{N}
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
              of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              (number of points) and consider the Fulton-MacPherson compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FM_n(\mathbb{R}^d)
              from Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FultonMacPhersonCompactification"}
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FM
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FM_n\left( \mathbb{R}^d\right)
              is, as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebras"} graded-commutative algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+algebra"} quotient algebra
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutative+algebra"} graded commutative algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
              by the classes of the forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i j}
              from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SphereClassGeneratorsOfDeRhamCohomology"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi FM
                        %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi d
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %mrow
                        %mo [
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi i
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^\bullet_{dR}\left(
                    FM_n\left( \mathbb{R}^d \right)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\wedge_{\mathbb{R}}^\bullet
                    \\left\langle
                    \\left[g_{i j}\right] \;\vert\; i \neq j \in \{1, \cdots, n\}
                    \\right\rangle / \sim
            %p
              by the following three relations (for all distinct
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j,k \in \{1,\cdots, n\}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mi i
                          %mo ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left[g_{i j}\right] \;\sim\; (-1)^d \left[g_{j i}\right]
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left[g_{i j}\right] \wedge \left[g_{i j}\right] \;\sim\; 0
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mi k
                          %mo ]
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mi k
                          %mo ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mi i
                          %mo ]
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mi i
                          %mo ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left[g_{i j}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{j k} \right]
                        +
                        \\left[g_{j k}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{k i} \right]
                        +
                        \\left[g_{k i}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{i j} \right]
                        \\;\sim\;
                        0
                  = succeed "(\u201C3-term" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\;\;\;
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Arnold69"}> Arnold 69
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Cohen73"} Cohen 73
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "configuration+space+of+points#Cohomology"} Cohomology
          #RealCohomologyOfFMCompactificationInTermsOfGraphCohomology.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
                of the FM-compactification in terms of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+cohomology"} graph cohomology
            %p
              In the
              = succeed "-model" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+type"} rational homotopy type
              of the ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Conf
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf_n\big( \mathbb{R}^D\big)
              the three relations in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeRhamCohomologyOfFMCompactification"}
              are incarnated as follows:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a graph changes sign when one of its edges is reversed (
                  %a{:href => "graph+complex#SignRulesForGraphs"}> this Def.
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  a graph with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+edges"} parallel edges
                  is a vanishing graph (
                  %a{:href => "graph+complex#VanishingGraphs"}> this Def.
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  the graph coboundary of a single trivalent internal vertex (
                  %a{:href => "graph+complex#ThreeTermRelation"}> this Example
                  ).
          %h3#RelationToGraphComplexes Relation to Graph complexes and Formality theorem
          %p
            We have that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+Fulton-MacPherson+operad+is+formal"} the Fulton-MacPherson operad is formal
            in the sense that for each of its component
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
