            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FultonMacPhersonCompactification"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            between their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            and their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cooperad"} cooperad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on both sides.
          %p
            Concretely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zags"} zig-zags
            may be taken to consist of one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            out of a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+operad"} Fulton-MacPherson operad
          %p
            Here the morphism from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+operad"} Fulton-MacPherson operad
            regards the latter as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphs"} graphs
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            and proceeds by sending each such graph/Feynman diagram to a corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitude"} Feynman amplitude
          %p
            This idea of a proof was sketched in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich99"} Kontsevich 99
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14
          #TheGraphComplexdgcAlgebra.num_defn
